/-!
# Outside-component selection in the radical argument

The imported reduction proves that the component selected in either surviving
1.3.4 alternative lies outside M, and combines this with the proved
normalization and C.2.3 construction. The initial overgroup's noncontainment
remains a separate obligation before the full selection theorem can be
assembled from the given quasisimple local overgroup.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
proof of Proposition 1.3.8, printed pp.513–514.
-/
